# No Pass-Through Wrappers

**YAGNI for forwarding-only types** — not a ban on utilities. Base-game `master` has many focused helpers (`GLog`, `PathFinder`, `GameMath`, `DeviceCompat`) that own real behavior. Keep that model on `main`.

## Reject

A new type whose public API **only** forwards to another type, or forces the caller to look up the same data twice.

- One-line facades (`prefetch(d)` → `Dungeon.prefetch…(d)`)
- “Service” / locator that only `new`s a composite and holds a static
- Config that only re-exposes another config’s getters
- `shouldX(lookup)` then `resolveX(lookup)` in the same flow (double fetch)

## Prefer

| Instead of                           | Do                                                        |
| ------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------- |
| Prefetch facade                      | Caller/scene calls the owner (`Dungeon`, storage, client) |
| Factory that only builds a singleton | `static` on the real type                                 |
| One-off JSON/health helper           | Private/package method on the owner                       |
| Duplicate filter + resolve           | One resolve path; callers use the result                  |

## Allowed thin types

- **Real policy / routing** (ranked vs local, mode selection)
- **Async / lifecycle** (executor, probe cache, upload queue)
- **Testable I/O seams** (HTTP transport interface + impl)
- **Multi-caller API** with non-trivial shared logic
- **Value objects** (results, policies, DTOs)
- **Master-style utils** that encapsulate algorithms or platform checks

## Before adding a class

1. Name the **extra behavior** in one sentence. If you can’t, inline.
2. One call site → private method on the caller/owner.
3. Collapse double lookups in the same flow.
4. Prefer extending an existing owner over a new `*Service` / `*Helper` / `*Prefetch`.
